 "help": "usage: wgsextract score pgs [-h] [--download | --no-download] --build {GRCh37,GRCh38}\n                            [--pgs-id PGS_ID | --trait TRAIT] [--scoring-file SCORING_FILE]\n                            [--sample SAMPLE] [--plink2-check]\n                            [--keep-ambiguous | --no-keep-ambiguous]\n                            [--confident-bed CONFIDENT_BED] [--min-match MIN_MATCH]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --download, --no-download\n                        Allow missing public reference/model downloads; no sample files or\n                        genotypes are uploaded. Hosts and request data: docs/privacy.md. Default:\n                        config allow_reference_downloads, else off.\n  --build {GRCh37,GRCh38}\n                        Input/scoring coordinate build (must match).\n  --pgs-id PGS_ID       Catalog PGS ID; uncurated IDs carry a warning.\n  --trait TRAIT         Curated trait (see docs/pgs.md).\n  --scoring-file SCORING_FILE\n                        Own scoring TSV[.gz], overriding Catalog selection.\n  --sample SAMPLE       VCF sample name (required for multi-sample files).\n  --plink2-check        Cross-check the matched-set sum with installed plink2 (no imputation).\n  --keep-ambiguous, --no-keep-ambiguous\n                        Keep A/T and C/G SNPs only if their forward strand was independently\n                        verified.\n  --confident-bed CONFIDENT_BED\n                        Same-sample/build confident BED: absent SNPs within it are reference calls\n                        (needs --ref).\n  --min-match MIN_MATCH\n                        Minimum matched fraction for percentile eligibility (default 0.75).\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract score pgs --input sample.vcf.gz --build GRCh38 --trait height\n  wgsextract score pgs --input sample.vcf.gz --build GRCh38 --pgs-id PGS000018\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  <input stem>_<PGS ID>_pgs.json and .tsv: raw score, variant match rate,\n  licence and citation; for curated GRCh38 scores, an ancestry-adjusted\n  percentile.\n\nneeds:\n  bcftools; depending on options and inputs, also: plink2, curl; minutes on a\n  30x genome.\n",
